  "accessionCode": "CCX-A-31079",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A block of pan crust, cut on three faces and lifted whole from the outer edge of the workings four days before a flood, with the cutting still unfinished at one corner. The upper surface carries nine cuts at four depths, made over about a week by one worker who was observed throughout and who neither objected to nor acknowledged the observation. It has been kept dry since 2294 and is the only block of its kind not to have been flooded, which means it is the only statement of this kind still standing. What it says is recorded in the field notes as not established.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
